>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `register_substrate`

``` hol4
Refute.register_substrate : substrate -> unit
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Adds or replaces an executable Quickcheck substrate.

The public type is an alias for this record:

``` hol4
type substrate =
  {name : string,
   priority : int,
   compile : Refute_Core.config -> Refute_Eval.strategy ->
     Refute_Eval.qc_problem -> Refute_Eval.compile_result}
```

Registrations are session-local.  The newest registration with a given
`name` replaces the old one.  `Auto` tries configured substrates by
increasing `priority`, then name; an explicitly selected built-in
substrate is selected by its name.

`compile` receives the common test plan and returns either
`Refute_Eval.Inapplicable reasons`, allowing `Auto` to continue, or a
`Compiled` test.  A substrate must preserve specified candidate order and
random-stream consumption, report exhaustion accurately, maintain its
statistics, and make the compiled test's `close` callback release all
resources on every exit path.

### See also

[`Refute.register_generator`](#Refute.register_generator),
[`Refute.register_backend`](#Refute.register_backend),
[`Refute.quickcheck`](#Refute.quickcheck),
[`Refute.config`](#Refute.config)

The substrate ladder is described in \ref{Description:the-holrefute-library}.
